<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Saint-Germain-en-Laye (1919)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1919">1919</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Treaty of Saint-Germain · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Saint-Germain-en-Laye was the peace treaty signed on 10 September 1919 between the Allied powers and the new Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It confirmed the break-up of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a>, recognised the independence of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and the Kingdom of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croats">Croats</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenes">Slovenes</a>, gave <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-tyrol">South Tyrol</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and forbade union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. It also assigned German-speaking western Hungary, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgenland">Burgenland</a>, to Austria.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saint-germain-en-laye-1919.jpg" alt="Treaty of Saint-Germain-en-Laye (1919)" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TratadoDeSaintGermainRenner.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
